      "content": "hey, i'm working on a loft addition for a client in oregon. we're using douglas fir for the main support. i need to figure out the span for a heavy beam to hold up the new floor, but i'm worried about deflection and if there are any specific load distribution rules i should be looking at for timber framing. what's the best way to calculate this to make sure the floor doesn't feel bouncy or sag over time?",
