      "content": "thanks. the L/240 limit makes sense. my main worry though is stuff i can't see once the walls are up. like, if there's a knot or a crack deep in the grain of the fir that i miss during inspection, could that cause a sudden failure or just more deflection? how do i account for those kinds of internal flaws in my math so i'm not just guessing?",
